    "details": "<p><strong>About Opencode:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Opencode is an open-source <strong>hackathon </strong>organized by Geekhaven.</li>\n<li>Designed to help students start their journey in the world of open source.</li>\n<li>Aims to foster innovation, collaboration, and contributions to open-source projects across various domains.</li>\n<li>Suitable for both beginners and experienced coders.</li>\n<li>Provides a platform to enhance skills, work with cutting-edge technologies, and engage with the open-source community.</li>\n<li>Communication will be conducted on <strong>Discord</strong>, and participants are encouraged to maintain a friendly and collaborative approach, especially on <strong>GitHub</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Tech Stacks:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Web Development:</strong> React, Node, Express, MongoDB, Spring Boot.</li>\n<li><strong>App Development:</strong> Flutter, Kotlin.</li>\n<li><strong>Design:</strong> Figma, UI/UX, Prototyping, Wireframing, Typography.</li>\n<li><strong>AI/ML:</strong> Python, PyTorch, TensorFlow, LLaMA.</li>\n<li><strong>Cybersecurity</strong>.</li>\n<li><strong>Game Development:</strong> Unity.</li>\n<li><strong>Blockchain</strong>.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Rules and Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<p><strong>Participation:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Individual participation only; no teams allowed.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Communication:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>All discussions and updates will take place on <strong>Discord</strong>.</li>\n<li>Participants must maintain respect, inclusivity, and collaboration at all times.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Submission Guidelines:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Pull requests must be submitted via <strong>GitHub repositories</strong>.</li>\n<li>Each submission must include:\n<ul>\n<li>A well-documented <code>README.md</code>.</li>\n<li>Proper project structure and commits.</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Commit messages should be clear and descriptive.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Project Requirements:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Follow the selected tech stack.</li>\n<li>Adhere to open-source contribution guidelines.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Code of Conduct:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Maintain a positive and constructive environment on <strong>GitHub</strong> and <strong>Discord</strong>.</li>\n<li>Avoid plagiarism and respect others' contributions.</li>\n<li>Follow the Contributor Guidelines at all times.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Evaluation Criteria:</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Code Quality:</strong> Creativity and impact.</li>\n<li><strong>Tech Stack Usage:</strong> Appropriate use of selected stacks.</li>\n<li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Active participation and GitHub activity.</li>\n<li><strong>UI/UX:</strong> Design and documentation quality.</li>\n</ul>",
    "end_date": "2026-12-13T23:00:00+05:30",
